/-!
# Enlarging a big site of schemes

For each of the five topologies that have big sites — Zariski, étale, smooth, syntomic and
fppf — a big site contained in a larger one of the same kind induces morphisms of topoi in
both directions whose composite retracts to the identity, and the same holds after localizing
at a scheme of the smaller site.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigSite` — the big site of a given topology, as an indexed family over
  `AlgebraicGeometry.CoveringTopology`, together with `AlgebraicGeometry.cutoff`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.siteCategory`, `AlgebraicGeometry.siteTopology` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.isCovering`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.IsContained` — one big site being contained in another, and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.inclusion` the resulting full inclusion of categories.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.base`, `AlgebraicGeometry.largerContains`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.overTopology` and `AlgebraicGeometry.inclusionOver` — the same data after
  localizing at a scheme.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ToposRetraction` — a pair of morphisms of topoi induced by a functor,
  together with the natural isomorphism exhibiting one as a retraction of the other.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.abelianRestrictionOver` and `AlgebraicGeometry.abelianExtensionOver` —
  restriction of abelian sheaves to the smaller localized big site and the pullback extending
  them to the larger one.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.hasFiniteLimits_siteCategory` — every big site has a terminal object and
  fibre products; for a localized big site this is the slice-category instance.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.generate_mem_siteTopology` — the sieve generated by a chosen covering
  family of a big site is a covering sieve for the site's topology.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.inclusion_isCocontinuous`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.inclusion_isMorphismOfSites` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.inclusion_preservesFiniteLimits`, with their `inclusionOver` analogues,
  are the site-level properties of the inclusion.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.toposRetraction` and `AlgebraicGeometry.toposRetractionOver` are the
  resulting retractions of topoi.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.abelianExtensionOverRestrictionIso` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_extension_abelianSheaf` — every abelian sheaf on the smaller
  localized big site is the restriction, up to isomorphism, of one on the larger.

## Implementation notes

The five big-site constructions are five different record types sharing one model: a cutoff
category of schemes together with a set-sized class of covering families. Indexing them by
`AlgebraicGeometry.CoveringTopology` states the result once without identifying sites of
different topologies — `AlgebraicGeometry.BigSite` is a genuine family, not a common
superclass, and `AlgebraicGeometry.cutoff`, `siteTopology` and `isCovering` are defined by
cases on the topology.

Only cocontinuity of the inclusion is proved by cases: for each topology it needs that a
covering family of the larger site at an object of the smaller one is refined by a covering
family of the smaller one, which is a different theorem in each case (Stacks 03WV, 03WW, 03WZ,
03X2, 03WX respectively). Everything else is uniform.

A retraction is recorded as `AlgebraicGeometry.ToposRetraction` rather than as an equality of
morphisms of topoi; its two `pushforward_iso` fields pin the two morphisms down to the ones
induced by the inclusion, so the structure is not merely asserting that some retraction
exists.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 022K](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/022K)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 00XU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00XU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03YY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03YY)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry Cardinal

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

private theorem schemeTerminal_size_lt (κ : Cardinal.{u}) (hκ : ℵ₀ < κ) :
    (⊤_ Scheme.{u}).size < κ := by
  have hsize : (⊤_ Scheme.{u}).size = Cardinal.aleph0 := by
    calc
      (⊤_ Scheme.{u}).size = (Spec (CommRingCat.of (ULift.{u} ℤ))).size :=
        Scheme.size_congr (IsTerminal.uniqueUpToIso terminalIsTerminal specULiftZIsTerminal)
      _ = max Cardinal.aleph0 (Cardinal.mk (ULift.{u} ℤ)) :=
        Scheme.size_Spec (CommRingCat.of (ULift.{u} ℤ))
      _ = Cardinal.aleph0 := by simp
  rwa [hsize]

public theorem schemeSizeBelow_closedUnderTerminal (κ : Cardinal.{u}) (hκ : ℵ₀ < κ) :
    (schemeSizeBelow κ).IsClosedUnderLimitsOfShape (Discrete.{0} PEmpty) := by
  apply ObjectProperty.IsClosedUnderLimitsOfShape.mk'
  rintro _ ⟨F, _⟩
  have ht : IsTerminal (limit F) :=
    (isLimitEquivIsTerminalOfIsEmpty Scheme (J := Discrete.{0} PEmpty) (F := F)
      (limit.cone F)) (limit.isLimit F)
  show (limit F).size < κ
  rw [Scheme.size_congr (ht.uniqueUpToIso terminalIsTerminal)]
  exact schemeTerminal_size_lt κ hκ

public theorem schemeSizeBelow_hasFiniteLimits (κ : Cardinal.{u}) (hκ : ℵ₀ < κ) :
    HasFiniteLimits (SchemeBelow κ) := by
  let P := schemeSizeBelow κ
  let : P.IsClosedUnderLimitsOfShape WalkingCospan :=
    schemeSizeBelow_isClosedUnderLimitsOfShape_walkingCospan κ
  let : P.IsClosedUnderLimitsOfShape (Discrete.{0} PEmpty) :=
    schemeSizeBelow_closedUnderTerminal κ hκ
  let : HasTerminal (SchemeBelow κ) := inferInstance
  let : HasPullbacks (SchemeBelow κ) := inferInstance
  exact hasFiniteLimits_of_hasTerminal_and_pullbacks

/-- A big site of the given topology: a big Zariski, étale, smooth, syntomic or fppf site,
according to `τ`. -/
public def BigSite : CoveringTopology → Type (u + 2)
  | .zariski => BigZariskiSite.{u}
  | .etale => BigEtaleSite.{u}
  | .smooth => BigSmoothSite.{u}
  | .syntomic => BigSyntomicSite.{u}
  | .fppf => BigFppfSite.{u}

/-- The cardinal cutting the category of all schemes down to the underlying category of a big
site. -/
public def cutoff : (τ : CoveringTopology) → BigSite.{u} τ → Cardinal.{u}
  | .zariski, B => B.schemeCardinal
  | .etale, B => B.cutoff
  | .smooth, B => B.cutoff
  | .syntomic, B => B.cutoff
  | .fppf, B => B.cutoff

private theorem aleph0_lt_cutoff (τ : CoveringTopology) (B : BigSite.{u} τ) :
    ℵ₀ < cutoff τ B := by
  cases τ with
  | zariski => exact B.aleph0_lt_schemeCardinal
  | etale => exact B.aleph0_lt_cutoff
  | smooth => exact B.aleph0_lt_cutoff
  | syntomic => exact B.aleph0_lt_cutoff
  | fppf => exact B.aleph0_lt_cutoff

/-- The underlying category of a big site: the schemes below its cutoff. -/
public abbrev siteCategory {τ : CoveringTopology} (B : BigSite.{u} τ) :=
  SchemeBelow (cutoff τ B)

/-- The Grothendieck topology of a big site. -/
public def siteTopology : (τ : CoveringTopology) → (B : BigSite.{u} τ) →
    GrothendieckTopology (siteCategory B)
  | .zariski, B => B.grothendieckTopology
  | .etale, B => B.topology
  | .smooth, B => B.grothendieckTopology
  | .syntomic, B => B.topology
  | .fppf, B => B.topology

/-- The distinguished covering families of a big site. -/
public def isCovering : (τ : CoveringTopology) → (B : BigSite.{u} τ) →
    Covering (siteCategory B) → Prop
  | .zariski, B => B.IsCovering
  | .etale, B => B.IsCovering
  | .smooth, B => B.IsCovering
  | .syntomic, B => B.IsCovering
  | .fppf, B => B.IsCovering

/-- The full inclusion of the underlying category of a big site into that of a big site with a
larger cutoff. -/
public abbrev inclusion {τ : CoveringTopology} {B B' : BigSite.{u} τ}
    (h : schemeSizeBelow (cutoff τ B) ≤
      schemeSizeBelow (cutoff τ B')) : siteCategory B ⥤ siteCategory B' :=
  ObjectProperty.ιOfLE (P := schemeSizeBelow (cutoff τ B))
    (P' := schemeSizeBelow (cutoff τ B'))
    h

/-- A big site is contained in another of the same topology when its cutoff is no larger and
every one of its distinguished covering families is one of the larger site's. -/
public def IsContained {τ : CoveringTopology} (B B' : BigSite.{u} τ) : Prop :=
  ∃ h : schemeSizeBelow (cutoff τ B) ≤
      schemeSizeBelow (cutoff τ B'),
    ∀ E : Covering (siteCategory B), isCovering τ B E →
      isCovering τ B' ⟨(inclusion h).obj E.1, E.2.map (inclusion h)⟩

private def sitePrecoverage (τ : CoveringTopology) (B : BigSite.{u} τ) :
    Precoverage (siteCategory B) := by
  cases τ with
  | zariski => exact B.precoverage
  | etale => exact B.precoverage
  | smooth => exact B.precoverage
  | syntomic => exact B.precoverage
  | fppf => exact B.precoverage

private theorem siteTopology_eq_precoverage (τ : CoveringTopology) (B : BigSite.{u} τ) :
    siteTopology τ B = (sitePrecoverage τ B).toGrothendieck := by
  cases τ <;> rfl

private def siteInclusion (τ : CoveringTopology) (B : BigSite.{u} τ) :
    siteCategory B ⥤ Scheme.{u} :=
  schemeBelowInclusion (cutoff τ B)

private theorem sitePrecoverage_mem_iff (τ : CoveringTopology) (B : BigSite.{u} τ)
    {X : siteCategory B} {R : Presieve X} :
    R ∈ sitePrecoverage τ B X ↔
      ∃ E : PreZeroHypercover X, isCovering τ B ⟨X, E⟩ ∧ R = E.presieve₀ := by
  cases τ with
  | zariski => rfl
  | smooth => rfl
  | etale | syntomic | fppf =>
      constructor <;> rintro ⟨E, h₁, h₂⟩ <;> exact ⟨E, h₂, h₁⟩

/-- The chosen covering families of a big site satisfy the site axioms. -/
public theorem siteCoverings_isSite (τ : CoveringTopology) (B : BigSite.{u} τ) :
    IsSite (isCovering τ B) := by
  cases τ with
  | zariski => exact B.coverings_isSite
  | etale => exact B.coverings_isSite
  | smooth => exact B.covering_isSite
  | syntomic => exact B.covering_isSite
  | fppf => exact B.coverings_isSite

private theorem exists_siteCovering_refining_sieve (τ : CoveringTopology)
    (B : BigSite.{u} τ) {X : siteCategory B} {R : Sieve X}
    (hR : R ∈ siteTopology τ B X) :
    ∃ E : PreZeroHypercover X, isCovering τ B ⟨X, E⟩ ∧ E.presieve₀ ≤ R := by
  rw [siteTopology_eq_precoverage] at hR
  exact CategoryTheory.exists_covering_refining_sieve (isCovering τ B) (sitePrecoverage τ B)
    (sitePrecoverage_mem_iff τ B).mp (siteCoverings_isSite τ B) hR

/-- Each chosen covering family of a big site generates a covering sieve. -/
public theorem generate_mem_siteTopology (τ : CoveringTopology) (B : BigSite.{u} τ)
    {X : siteCategory B} (E : PreZeroHypercover X)
    (hE : isCovering τ B ⟨X, E⟩) :
    Sieve.generate E.presieve₀ ∈ siteTopology τ B X := by
  rw [siteTopology_eq_precoverage]
  exact (sitePrecoverage τ B).generate_mem_toGrothendieck
    ((sitePrecoverage_mem_iff τ B).mpr ⟨E, hE, rfl⟩)

private theorem inclusion_cocontinuous_of_refinement {τ : CoveringTopology}
    {B B' : BigSite.{u} τ}
    (hSize : schemeSizeBelow (cutoff τ B) ≤
      schemeSizeBelow (cutoff τ B')) {X : siteCategory B}
    {R : Sieve ((inclusion hSize).obj X)}
    {E : PreZeroHypercover ((inclusion hSize).obj X)}
    (hER : E.presieve₀ ≤ R) {V : PreZeroHypercover X}
    (hV : isCovering τ B ⟨X, V⟩)
    (hRef : Nonempty ((V.map (siteInclusion τ B)).Hom
      (E.map (siteInclusion τ B')))) :
    R.functorPullback (inclusion hSize) ∈ siteTopology τ B X := by
  classical
  let F := inclusion hSize
  refine (siteTopology τ B).superset_covering ?_ (generate_mem_siteTopology τ B V hV)
  rw [Sieve.generate_le_iff, Presieve.ofArrows_le_iff]
  intro i
  obtain ⟨φ⟩ := hRef
  let j : E.I₀ := φ.s₀ i
  let e' := siteInclusion τ B'
  have : e'.Full := by
    dsimp [e', siteInclusion, schemeBelowInclusion]
    infer_instance
  have : e'.Faithful := by
    dsimp [e', siteInclusion, schemeBelowInclusion]
    infer_instance
  let eComp : F ⋙ e' ≅ siteInclusion τ B :=
    ObjectProperty.ιOfLECompιIso hSize
  let g : F.obj (V.X i) ⟶ E.X j :=
    e'.preimage (eComp.hom.app (V.X i) ≫ φ.h₀ i)
  have hg : e'.map g = eComp.hom.app (V.X i) ≫ φ.h₀ i := e'.map_preimage _
  have hfactor : g ≫ E.f j = F.map (V.f i) :=
    e'.map_injective (by
      rw [Functor.map_comp, hg]
      exact (Category.assoc _ _ _).trans ((Category.id_comp _).trans (φ.w₀ i)))
  show R.arrows (F.map (V.f i))
  rw [← hfactor]
  exact R.downward_closed (hER _ _ ⟨j⟩) g

private theorem inclusion_coverPreserving {τ : CoveringTopology}
    {B B' : BigSite.{u} τ}
    (hSize : schemeSizeBelow (cutoff τ B) ≤
      schemeSizeBelow (cutoff τ B'))
    (hCover : ∀ E : Covering (siteCategory B), isCovering τ B E →
      isCovering τ B' ⟨(inclusion hSize).obj E.1, E.2.map (inclusion hSize)⟩) :
    CoverPreserving (siteTopology τ B) (siteTopology τ B') (inclusion hSize) := by
  classical
  let F := inclusion hSize
  constructor
  intro X R hR
  obtain ⟨E, hE, hER⟩ := exists_siteCovering_refining_sieve τ B hR
  refine (siteTopology τ B').superset_covering ?_
    (generate_mem_siteTopology τ B' (E.map F) (hCover ⟨X, E⟩ hE))
  rw [Sieve.generate_le_iff, Presieve.ofArrows_le_iff]
  exact fun i => R.image_mem_functorPushforward F (hER _ _ ⟨i⟩)

/-- The underlying category of any of the five big sites has a terminal object
and fibre products. -/
@[stacks 022K "existence of finite limits in the big sites"]
public instance hasFiniteLimits_siteCategory {τ : CoveringTopology}
    (B : BigSite.{u} τ) : HasFiniteLimits (siteCategory B) :=
  schemeSizeBelow_hasFiniteLimits (cutoff τ B) (aleph0_lt_cutoff τ B)

add_to_stacks 022K "existence of finite limits in localized big sites"
  CategoryTheory.Over.hasFiniteLimits

@[stacks 022K "the inclusion is cocontinuous"]
public theorem inclusion_isCocontinuous {τ : CoveringTopology}
    (B B' : BigSite.{u} τ) (h : IsContained B B') :
    (inclusion (Classical.choose h)).IsCocontinuous (siteTopology τ B) (siteTopology τ B') := by
  classical
  let hSize := Classical.choose h
  constructor
  intro X R hR
  obtain ⟨E, hE, hER⟩ := exists_siteCovering_refining_sieve τ B' hR
  cases τ with
  | zariski =>
      let U0 := E.map (siteInclusion .zariski B')
      let U : (B.inclusion.obj X).OpenCover := {
        __ := U0
        mem₀ := by
          show U0.presieve₀ ∈ Scheme.zariskiPretopology (B.inclusion.obj X)
          exact hE.1 }
      obtain ⟨V, hV, hEquiv⟩ :=
        BigZariskiSite.exists_isCovering_tautologicallyEquivalent_openCover B X U
      have hRef : Nonempty ((V.map B.inclusion).Hom (E.map B'.inclusion)) :=
        (PreZeroHypercover.nonempty_hom_and_nonempty_hom_of_tautologicallyEquivalent
          U.toPreZeroHypercover (V.map B.inclusion) hEquiv).2
      exact inclusion_cocontinuous_of_refinement hSize hER hV hRef
  | etale =>
      obtain ⟨V, hV, hRef⟩ := BigEtaleSite.exists_covering_refining_etale_cover B (T := X)
        (E.map (siteInclusion .etale B')) hE.1
      exact inclusion_cocontinuous_of_refinement hSize hER hV hRef
  | smooth =>
      obtain ⟨V, hV, hRef⟩ :=
        exists_covering_refining_smooth_cover B (T := X) (E.map (siteInclusion .smooth B')) hE.1
      exact inclusion_cocontinuous_of_refinement hSize hER hV hRef
  | syntomic =>
      obtain ⟨V, hV, hRef⟩ :=
        exists_siteCovering_refining B X (E.map (siteInclusion .syntomic B')) hE.1
      exact inclusion_cocontinuous_of_refinement hSize hER hV hRef
  | fppf =>
      let U := E.map (siteInclusion .fppf B')
      have hU : U.presieve₀ ∈ Scheme.fppfPrecoverage
          ((siteInclusion .fppf B).obj X) := by
        have hh := BigFppfSite.isFppfCovering_of_isCovering B' hE
        change E.presieve₀ ∈ Scheme.fppfPrecoverage.comap
          (schemeBelowInclusion (cutoff .fppf B')) ((inclusion hSize).obj X) at hh
        rw [Precoverage.mem_comap_iff] at hh
        show (E.map (siteInclusion .fppf B')).presieve₀ ∈
          Scheme.fppfPrecoverage ((siteInclusion .fppf B').obj ((inclusion hSize).obj X))
        rwa [PreZeroHypercover.presieve₀_map]
      obtain ⟨V, hV, hRef⟩ :=
        exists_isCovering_refining_fppfCovering B X U hU
      exact inclusion_cocontinuous_of_refinement hSize hER hV hRef

@[stacks 022K "the inclusion preserves finite limits"]
public theorem inclusion_preservesFiniteLimits {τ : CoveringTopology}
    (B B' : BigSite.{u} τ) (h : IsContained B B') :
    PreservesFiniteLimits (inclusion (Classical.choose h)) := by
  let P := schemeSizeBelow (cutoff τ B)
  let P' := schemeSizeBelow (cutoff τ B')
  let F := inclusion (Classical.choose h)
  have : P.IsClosedUnderLimitsOfShape WalkingCospan :=
    schemeSizeBelow_isClosedUnderLimitsOfShape_walkingCospan (cutoff τ B)
  have : P'.IsClosedUnderLimitsOfShape WalkingCospan :=
    schemeSizeBelow_isClosedUnderLimitsOfShape_walkingCospan (cutoff τ B')
  have : P.IsClosedUnderLimitsOfShape (Discrete.{0} PEmpty) :=
    schemeSizeBelow_closedUnderTerminal (cutoff τ B) (aleph0_lt_cutoff τ B)
  have : P'.IsClosedUnderLimitsOfShape (Discrete.{0} PEmpty) :=
    schemeSizeBelow_closedUnderTerminal (cutoff τ B') (aleph0_lt_cutoff τ B')
  have : ReflectsLimitsOfShape (Discrete.{0} PEmpty) P'.ι := inferInstance
  have : ReflectsLimitsOfShape WalkingCospan P'.ι := inferInstance
  have : PreservesLimitsOfShape (Discrete.{0} PEmpty) (F ⋙ P'.ι) :=
    preservesLimitsOfShape_of_natIso (ObjectProperty.ιOfLECompιIso (Classical.choose h)).symm
  have : PreservesLimitsOfShape WalkingCospan (F ⋙ P'.ι) :=
    preservesLimitsOfShape_of_natIso (ObjectProperty.ιOfLECompιIso (Classical.choose h)).symm
  have : PreservesLimitsOfShape (Discrete.{0} PEmpty) F :=
    preservesLimitsOfShape_of_reflects_of_preserves F P'.ι
  have : PreservesLimitsOfShape WalkingCospan F :=
    preservesLimitsOfShape_of_reflects_of_preserves F P'.ι
  exact preservesFiniteLimits_of_preservesTerminal_and_pullbacks F

/-- A cover-preserving, finite-limit-preserving functor out of a finitely complete site is a
morphism of sites. -/
private theorem isMorphismOfSites_of_coverPreserving {C D : Type (u + 1)} [Category.{u} C]
    [Category.{u} D] [HasFiniteLimits C] (F : C ⥤ D) [PreservesFiniteLimits F]
    (J : GrothendieckTopology C) (K : GrothendieckTopology D) (hF : CoverPreserving J K F) :
    _root_.IsMorphismOfSites.{u + 1} F J K := by
  have : RepresentablyFlat F := flat_of_preservesFiniteLimits F
  have : F.IsContinuous J K :=
    Functor.isContinuous_of_coverPreserving (compatiblePreservingOfFlat K F) hF
  have : PreservesFiniteLimits (F.op.lan :
      (Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type (u + 1)) ⥤ Dᵒᵖ ⥤ Type (u + 1)) :=
    CategoryTheory.lan_preservesFiniteLimits_of_representablyFlat.{u, u, u + 1, u + 1, u + 1} F
  exact
    { __ := (inferInstance : F.IsContinuous J K)
      hasExactLeftAdjoint :=
        ⟨F.sheafPullback (Type (u + 1)) J K, ⟨F.sheafAdjunctionContinuous (Type (u + 1)) J K⟩,
          Functor.sheafPullbackConstruction.preservesFiniteLimits F (Type (u + 1)) J K⟩ }

@[stacks 022K "the inclusion is a morphism of sites"]
public theorem inclusion_isMorphismOfSites {τ : CoveringTopology}
    (B B' : BigSite.{u} τ) (h : IsContained B B') :
    _root_.IsMorphismOfSites.{u + 1} (inclusion (Classical.choose h))
      (siteTopology τ B) (siteTopology τ B') := by
  classical
  have : PreservesFiniteLimits (inclusion (Classical.choose h)) :=
    inclusion_preservesFiniteLimits B B' h
  exact isMorphismOfSites_of_coverPreserving _ _ _
    (inclusion_coverPreserving _ (Classical.choose_spec h))

/-- A scheme below the cutoff, as an object of the underlying category of a big site. -/
public abbrev base {τ : CoveringTopology} (B : BigSite.{u} τ)
    (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : S.size < cutoff τ B) : siteCategory B := ⟨S, hS⟩

/-- The Grothendieck topology of a big site localized at a scheme. -/
public def overTopology : (τ : CoveringTopology) → (B : BigSite.{u} τ) →
    (S : Scheme.{u}) → (hS : S.size < cutoff τ B) →
      GrothendieckTopology (Over (base B S hS))
  | .zariski, B, S, hS => BigZariskiOver.topology B S hS
  | .etale, B, S, hS => BigEtaleOver.topology B S hS
  | .smooth, B, S, hS => BigSmoothOver.topology B S hS
  | .syntomic, B, S, hS => BigSyntomicOver.topology B S hS
  | .fppf, B, S, hS => BigFppfOver.topology B S hS

/-- A scheme below the cutoff of a big site is below the cutoff of any big site containing
it. -/
public abbrev largerContains {τ : CoveringTopology} {B B' : BigSite.{u} τ}
    (h : IsContained B B') {S : Scheme.{u}}
    (hS : S.size < cutoff τ B) : S.size < cutoff τ B' :=
  (Classical.choose h) S hS

/-- The full inclusion of a localized big site into the localization of a big site containing
it. -/
public abbrev inclusionOver {τ : CoveringTopology} {B B' : BigSite.{u} τ}
    (h : IsContained B B') (S : Scheme.{u})
    (hS : S.size < cutoff τ B) :
    Over (base B S hS) ⥤ Over (base B' S (largerContains h hS)) :=
  Over.post (inclusion (Classical.choose h))

/-- The topology of a localized big site is the localization of the topology of the big site. -/
public theorem overTopology_eq_over {τ : CoveringTopology}
    (B : BigSite.{u} τ) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : S.size < cutoff τ B) :
    overTopology τ B S hS = (siteTopology τ B).over (base B S hS) := by
  cases τ with
  | zariski => exact BigZariskiOver.topology_eq_over B ⟨S, hS⟩
  | etale => exact bigEtaleOver_topology_eq B S hS
  | smooth => rfl
  | syntomic => rfl
  | fppf => rfl

@[stacks 022K "the localized inclusion is cocontinuous"]
public theorem inclusionOver_isCocontinuous {τ : CoveringTopology}
    (B B' : BigSite.{u} τ) (h : IsContained B B')
    (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : S.size < cutoff τ B) :
    (inclusionOver h S hS).IsCocontinuous
      (overTopology τ B S hS)
      (overTopology τ B' S (largerContains h hS)) := by
  let hSize := Classical.choose h
  let F := inclusion hSize
  let J := siteTopology τ B
  let K := siteTopology τ B'
  let : F.IsCocontinuous J K := inclusion_isCocontinuous B B' h
  rw [overTopology_eq_over B S hS, overTopology_eq_over B' S (largerContains h hS)]
  show (Over.post (X := base B S hS) F).IsCocontinuous
    ((siteTopology τ B).over (base B S hS))
    ((siteTopology τ B').over (F.obj (base B S hS)))
  infer_instance

@[stacks 022K "the localized inclusion is a morphism of sites"]
public theorem inclusionOver_isMorphismOfSites {τ : CoveringTopology}
    (B B' : BigSite.{u} τ) (h : IsContained B B')
    (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : S.size < cutoff τ B) :
    _root_.IsMorphismOfSites.{u + 1} (inclusionOver h S hS)
      (overTopology τ B S hS)
      (overTopology τ B' S (largerContains h hS)) := by
  classical
  let : PreservesFiniteLimits (inclusion (Classical.choose h)) :=
    inclusion_preservesFiniteLimits B B' h
  let : PreservesFiniteLimits (inclusionOver h S hS) := by
    show PreservesFiniteLimits (Over.post (X := base B S hS) (inclusion (Classical.choose h)))
    infer_instance
  refine isMorphismOfSites_of_coverPreserving _ _ _ ?_
  rw [overTopology_eq_over, overTopology_eq_over]
  exact (inclusion_coverPreserving _ (Classical.choose_spec h)).overPost (base B S hS)

@[stacks 022K "the localized inclusion preserves finite limits"]
public theorem inclusionOver_preservesFiniteLimits {τ : CoveringTopology}
    (B B' : BigSite.{u} τ) (h : IsContained B B')
    (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : S.size < cutoff τ B) :
    PreservesFiniteLimits (inclusionOver h S hS) := by
  let F := inclusion (Classical.choose h)
  let : PreservesFiniteLimits F := inclusion_preservesFiniteLimits B B' h
  show PreservesFiniteLimits (Over.post (X := base B S hS) F)
  infer_instance

/-- A pair of morphisms of topoi induced by a continuous and cocontinuous functor, together
with the natural isomorphism exhibiting the composite of their direct images as the identity.

The two `pushforward_iso` fields pin the morphisms down to the ones the functor induces, so
that the structure asserts the retraction of *those* morphisms rather than the existence of
some retraction. -/
public structure ToposRetraction
    (C D : Type (u + 1)) [Category.{u} C] [Category.{u} D]
    (J : GrothendieckTopology C) (K : GrothendieckTopology D)
    (F : C ⥤ D) [F.IsCocontinuous J K] [F.IsContinuous J K] where
  /-- The morphism of topoi from the sheaves on the source site to those on the target. -/
  g : MorphismOfTopoi (Sheaf J (Type (u + 1))) (Sheaf K (Type (u + 1)))
  /-- The morphism of topoi back from the sheaves on the target site. -/
  f : MorphismOfTopoi (Sheaf K (Type (u + 1))) (Sheaf J (Type (u + 1)))
  /-- The direct image of `g` is the cocontinuous pushforward of the functor. -/
  g_pushforward_iso : g.pushforward ≅ F.sheafPushforwardCocontinuous (Type (u + 1)) J K
  /-- The direct image of `f` is the continuous pushforward of the functor. -/
  f_pushforward_iso : f.pushforward ≅ F.sheafPushforwardContinuous (Type (u + 1)) J K
  /-- The composite of the two direct images is the identity. -/
  retraction_iso : g.pushforward ⋙ f.pushforward ≅ 𝟭 _

@[stacks 022K "the retraction of big topoi"]
public noncomputable def toposRetraction {τ : CoveringTopology}
    (B B' : BigSite.{u} τ) (h : IsContained B B') :
    let J := siteTopology τ B
    let K := siteTopology τ B'
    let F := inclusion (Classical.choose h)
    let : F.IsCocontinuous J K := inclusion_isCocontinuous B B' h
    let : F.IsContinuous J K := (inclusion_isMorphismOfSites B B' h).toIsContinuous
    ToposRetraction (siteCategory B) (siteCategory B') J K F := by
  classical
  let J := siteTopology τ B
  let K := siteTopology τ B'
  let F := inclusion (Classical.choose h)
  let : F.IsCocontinuous J K := inclusion_isCocontinuous B B' h
  let : F.IsContinuous J K := (inclusion_isMorphismOfSites B B' h).toIsContinuous
  change ToposRetraction (siteCategory B) (siteCategory B') J K F
  let hSites := inclusion_isMorphismOfSites B B' h
  let : F.IsContinuous J K := hSites.toIsContinuous
  let : F.Full := by
    dsimp [F, inclusion]
    infer_instance
  let : F.Faithful := by
    dsimp [F, inclusion]
    infer_instance
  let adj := F.sheafAdjunctionCocontinuous (Type (u + 1)) J K
  let L := Classical.choose hSites.hasExactLeftAdjoint
  have hLspec := Classical.choose_spec hSites.hasExactLeftAdjoint
  let adjL := Classical.choice hLspec.1
  have hL := hLspec.2
  let g : MorphismOfTopoi (Sheaf J (Type (u + 1))) (Sheaf K (Type (u + 1))) :=
    { pushforward := F.sheafPushforwardCocontinuous (Type (u + 1)) J K
      inverseImage := F.sheafPushforwardContinuous (Type (u + 1)) J K
      adj := adj
      preservesFiniteLimits := inferInstance }
  let f : MorphismOfTopoi (Sheaf K (Type (u + 1))) (Sheaf J (Type (u + 1))) :=
    { pushforward := F.sheafPushforwardContinuous (Type (u + 1)) J K
      inverseImage := L
      adj := adjL
      preservesFiniteLimits := hL }
  refine ⟨g, f, Iso.refl _, Iso.refl _, ?_⟩
  let : IsIso adj.counit :=
    Functor.isIso_sheafAdjunctionCocontinuous_counit F (Type (u + 1)) J K
  exact asIso adj.counit

@[stacks 022K "the retraction of localized topoi"]
public noncomputable def toposRetractionOver {τ : CoveringTopology}
    (B B' : BigSite.{u} τ) (h : IsContained B B')
    (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : S.size < cutoff τ B) :
    let J := overTopology τ B S hS
    let K := overTopology τ B' S (largerContains h hS)
    let F := inclusionOver h S hS
    let : F.IsCocontinuous J K := inclusionOver_isCocontinuous B B' h S hS
    let : F.IsContinuous J K := (inclusionOver_isMorphismOfSites B B' h S hS).toIsContinuous
    ToposRetraction (Over (base B S hS))
      (Over (base B' S (largerContains h hS))) J K F := by
  classical
  let J := overTopology τ B S hS
  let K := overTopology τ B' S (largerContains h hS)
  let F := inclusionOver h S hS
  let : F.IsCocontinuous J K := inclusionOver_isCocontinuous B B' h S hS
  let : F.IsContinuous J K :=
    (inclusionOver_isMorphismOfSites B B' h S hS).toIsContinuous
  change ToposRetraction (Over (base B S hS))
    (Over (base B' S (largerContains h hS))) J K F
  let hSites := inclusionOver_isMorphismOfSites B B' h S hS
  let : F.IsContinuous J K := hSites.toIsContinuous
  let : (inclusion (Classical.choose h)).Full := by
    dsimp [inclusion]
    infer_instance
  let : (inclusion (Classical.choose h)).Faithful := by
    dsimp [inclusion]
    infer_instance
  let : F.Full := by
    change (Over.post (X := base B S hS) (inclusion (Classical.choose h))).Full
    infer_instance
  let : F.Faithful := by
    change (Over.post (X := base B S hS) (inclusion (Classical.choose h))).Faithful
    infer_instance
  let adj := F.sheafAdjunctionCocontinuous (Type (u + 1)) J K
  let L := Classical.choose hSites.hasExactLeftAdjoint
  have hLspec := Classical.choose_spec hSites.hasExactLeftAdjoint
  let adjL := Classical.choice hLspec.1
  have hL := hLspec.2
  let g : MorphismOfTopoi (Sheaf J (Type (u + 1))) (Sheaf K (Type (u + 1))) :=
    { pushforward := F.sheafPushforwardCocontinuous (Type (u + 1)) J K
      inverseImage := F.sheafPushforwardContinuous (Type (u + 1)) J K
      adj := adj
      preservesFiniteLimits := inferInstance }
  let f : MorphismOfTopoi (Sheaf K (Type (u + 1))) (Sheaf J (Type (u + 1))) :=
    { pushforward := F.sheafPushforwardContinuous (Type (u + 1)) J K
      inverseImage := L
      adj := adjL
      preservesFiniteLimits := hL }
  refine ⟨g, f, Iso.refl _, Iso.refl _, ?_⟩
  let : IsIso adj.counit :=
    Functor.isIso_sheafAdjunctionCocontinuous_counit F (Type (u + 1)) J K
  exact asIso adj.counit

/-! ### Abelian sheaves

The inclusion of a localized big site into a larger one is fully faithful, continuous and
cocontinuous, so Stacks 00XU applies to it: the pullback of abelian sheaves is fully faithful,
and the unit of the adjunction identifies an abelian sheaf with the restriction of its pullback.
-/

/-- The localized inclusion of a big site into a larger one is continuous. This is the
continuity half of `AlgebraicGeometry.inclusionOver_isMorphismOfSites`, as an instance, so that
the restriction functor on sheaves is available to instance search. -/
public instance inclusionOver_isContinuous {τ : CoveringTopology}
    (B B' : BigSite.{u} τ) (h : IsContained B B')
    (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : S.size < cutoff τ B) :
    (inclusionOver h S hS).IsContinuous
      (overTopology τ B S hS)
      (overTopology τ B' S (largerContains h hS)) :=
  (inclusionOver_isMorphismOfSites B B' h S hS).toIsContinuous

/-- The localized inclusion of a big site into a larger one is full: it is the inclusion of a
full subcategory of schemes, localized over a scheme of the smaller site. -/
public instance inclusionOver_full {τ : CoveringTopology} {B B' : BigSite.{u} τ}
    (h : IsContained B B') (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : S.size < cutoff τ B) :
    (inclusionOver h S hS).Full := by
  let : (inclusion (Classical.choose h)).Full := by
    dsimp [inclusion]
    infer_instance
  change (Over.post (X := base B S hS) (inclusion (Classical.choose h))).Full
  infer_instance

/-- The localized inclusion of a big site into a larger one is faithful. -/
public instance inclusionOver_faithful {τ : CoveringTopology} {B B' : BigSite.{u} τ}
    (h : IsContained B B') (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : S.size < cutoff τ B) :
    (inclusionOver h S hS).Faithful := by
  let : (inclusion (Classical.choose h)).Faithful := by
    dsimp [inclusion]
    infer_instance
  change (Over.post (X := base B S hS) (inclusion (Classical.choose h))).Faithful
  infer_instance

/-- Restriction of abelian sheaves from a localized big site to the localization of a big site
contained in it: the pushforward along the continuous `AlgebraicGeometry.inclusionOver`. -/
public abbrev abelianRestrictionOver {τ : CoveringTopology}
    (B B' : BigSite.{u} τ) (h : IsContained B B')
    (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : S.size < cutoff τ B) :
    Sheaf (overTopology τ B' S (largerContains h hS)) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} ⥤
      Sheaf (overTopology τ B S hS) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} :=
  (inclusionOver h S hS).sheafPushforwardContinuous AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}
    (overTopology τ B S hS) (overTopology τ B' S (largerContains h hS))

/-- The extension of an abelian sheaf on a localized big site to the localization of a larger
big site: the sheaf pullback along `AlgebraicGeometry.inclusionOver`. -/
public noncomputable def abelianExtensionOver {τ : CoveringTopology}
    (B B' : BigSite.{u} τ) (h : IsContained B B')
    (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : S.size < cutoff τ B)
    (F : Sheaf (overTopology τ B S hS) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}) :
    Sheaf (overTopology τ B' S (largerContains h hS)) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} :=
  ((inclusionOver h S hS).sheafPullback AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}
    (overTopology τ B S hS) (overTopology τ B' S (largerContains h hS))).obj F

/-- The restriction of `AlgebraicGeometry.abelianExtensionOver F` to the smaller localized big
site is `F` itself. The isomorphism is the inverse of the unit of the adjunction between pullback
and restriction, which is invertible because the pullback is fully faithful (Stacks 00XU). -/
public noncomputable def abelianExtensionOverRestrictionIso {τ : CoveringTopology}
    (B B' : BigSite.{u} τ) (h : IsContained B B')
    (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : S.size < cutoff τ B)
    (F : Sheaf (overTopology τ B S hS) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}) :
    (abelianRestrictionOver B B' h S hS).obj (abelianExtensionOver B B' h S hS F) ≅ F := by
  let G := inclusionOver h S hS
  let J := overTopology τ B S hS
  let K := overTopology τ B' S (largerContains h hS)
  let : G.IsCocontinuous J K := inclusionOver_isCocontinuous B B' h S hS
  let hff := Functor.full_and_faithful_sheafPullback G AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} J K
  let : (G.sheafPullback AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} J K).Full := hff.1
  let : (G.sheafPullback AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} J K).Faithful := hff.2
  exact (asIso ((G.sheafAdjunctionContinuous AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} J K).unit.app F)).symm

/-- **An abelian sheaf on a big site extends to any larger big site of the same topology.** For
nested big `τ`-sites over a scheme `S`, every abelian sheaf on the smaller localized site is the
restriction, up to isomorphism, of an abelian sheaf on the larger one. -/
@[stacks 03YY "extend_abelian_sheaf"]
public theorem exists_extension_abelianSheaf {τ : CoveringTopology}
    (B B' : BigSite.{u} τ) (h : IsContained B B')
    (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : S.size < cutoff τ B)
    (F : Sheaf (overTopology τ B S hS) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}) :
    ∃ F' : Sheaf (overTopology τ B' S (largerContains h hS)) AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1},
      Nonempty ((abelianRestrictionOver B B' h S hS).obj F' ≅ F) :=
  ⟨abelianExtensionOver B B' h S hS F,
    ⟨abelianExtensionOverRestrictionIso B B' h S hS F⟩⟩

end AlgebraicGeometry
